00:05:04,000 --> 00:05:10,000
Hulk vs. Wolverine is a animation, action, science
fiction film directed by Frank Paur.

3
00:07:36,000 --> 00:07:42,000
Department H sends in Wolverine to track down a mysterious beast known by the US
Military as the Hulk, who is rampaging across the Canadian wilderness.

4
00:10:08,000 --> 00:10:14,000
Surveying the extent of the damage to a destroyed town, Wolverine
notices a toxic scent as well as the smell of gunpowder.

5
00:12:40,000 --> 00:12:46,000
He is then deployed to the wilderness to resume tracking the creature.

6
00:15:12,000 --> 00:15:18,000
Hulk (voice), played by Fred Tatasciore.

7
00:17:44,000 --> 00:17:50,000
Bruce Banner (voice), played by Bryce Johnson.

8
00:20:16,000 --> 00:20:22,000
Wolverine / Logan (voice), played by Steve Blum.

9
00:22:48,000 --> 00:22:54,000
Deadpool (voice), played by Nolan North.

10
00:25:20,000 --> 00:25:26,000
The Professor (voice), played by Tom Kane.

11
00:27:52,000 --> 00:27:58,000
Lady Deathstrike (voice), played by Janyse Jaud.

12
00:30:24,000 --> 00:30:30,000
Marvel Animated Features (MAF) is a series of eight American direct-to-video animated superhero films made by MLG
Productions, a joint venture between Marvel Studios (later Marvel Animation) and Lions Gate Entertainment.

13
00:32:56,000 --> 00:33:02,000
The film explores themes of superhero, mutant, based on comic, norse mythology.

14
00:35:28,000 --> 00:35:34,000
The tone is thought_provoking.
